From ec6f9c480b7de187350672478500448e59a54ea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:04:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(launch): retain owned current directories per process

Use VFS directory references for chdir, fchdir and getcwd. Copy them
through fork, preserve them through exec, and retire them on successful
image cwd changes, failed reservations or death. Preserve native scratch
restoration and report renamed/removed directory identity accurately.

Signed-off-by: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
---
 README.md                                 |  15 ++-
 crates/ginux-init/src/fs_hooks.rs         |  84 ++++++++++++++---
 crates/ginux-init/src/launch_tasks.rs     | 109 +++++++++++++++++++---
 scripts/test-launch-directories.py        |   6 +-
 tests/fixtures/launch-directory-fixture.c |  72 ++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 252 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 9fffd909..b3dec331 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -238,11 +238,18 @@ chmod and stat/fstat/fstatat/statx metadata. Access and readlink probes stay in
 the owned namespace; regular files accept O_NOCTTY. Directory cookies and inode
 identity follow open descriptions across aliases, fork, rename and removal.
 Namespace changes validate types, capacity and replacement before mutation.
-Relative AT_FDCWD paths follow the calling process's image cwd; owned directory
+Relative AT_FDCWD paths follow the calling process's cwd; owned directory
 FDs resolve relative operations through their current VFS identity. Image chdir,
-getcwd and relative image exec retain native per-process cwd semantics. Entering
-owned directories as cwd, relative image-directory FD access, hardlinks and
-guest file mappings remain unsupported.
+getcwd and relative image exec retain native per-process cwd semantics.
+Relative image-directory FD access, hardlinks and guest file mappings remain
+unsupported. Owned chdir/fchdir/getcwd keep a private VFS directory reference per
+process. Fork copies that reference; exec keeps it; successful image chdir/fchdir
+releases it. Rename updates the reported path, and a removed cwd reports ENOENT
+for getcwd and relative operations until an absolute directory change. Private
+cwd references consume the existing 64-entry VFS open-description capacity.
+Relative owned scripts/interpreters use that cwd; relative fallback into the image
+and native kernel-selected relative interpreters from owned cwd remain unsupported.
+Configured-launch threads and shared cwd groups remain unsupported.
 Owned symlink/symlinkat and readlink/readlinkat support bounded targets and
 nofollow metadata. Link expansion precedes later parent components; mutations
 name the final link itself, including directory requirements on trailing slashes.
